    "added_after_the_run": true,
    "why_this_file_exists": "A re-run of the published 2026-08-29 experiment, kept as evidence rather than as a replacement. Every one of 32 measurements came back higher than the August run -- median 2.83x, range 2.13x to 3.62x -- and every one passed the harness's convergence check. The cause is the machine, not the code: on the same day the August harness, the current harness and stdlib timeit all agreed with each other and all disagreed with August by ~3x. results.json still holds the August run, which remains the fastest this machine has been observed to produce.",
